  "preprocessing/cv_extractor.v1.2.3.yaml": `version: "1.2.3"
description: "Transform CV text into a structured, schema-conforming semantic profile for LLM use; stable skills groupings on rerun."

prompt:
  role: "CV to semantic profile transformer"

  inputs:
    cv_text_for_extraction: "CV text used for extraction (raw upload text or serialized edited rerun text)."
    selected_missing_skills: "Optional candidate-selected skill tokens to fold into existing skills groups when provided."

  objective: >
    Semantic compression: remove redundancy and prose; convert narrative into keyword-style concepts; preserve all meaning.
    Output must match the provided JSON schema. This is not a human-readable CV or a summarisation - optimise for LLM consumption.

  rules:
    - "Include every item from the source in every section; do not skip or drop entries."
    - "Strip metadata (timestamps, runId, cached, additional_sections) and duplicated content only; keep all substantive content."
    - "When selected_missing_skills are present, for each skill first check whether an existing skills group is already suitable by theme (tools, cloud/platform, leadership, operations, architecture, domain, etc.). If suitable, add the skill there."
    - "Only create a new skills group for a selected_missing_skill when no existing group is reasonably suitable after that check. Never create duplicate or near-duplicate groups."
    - "Preserve existing skills group headings from the CV when they are present; prefer merging content into those groups over creating new parallel groups with similar meaning."
    - "Do not create skills group headings that describe learning plans, gaps, ramp-up, training, or development areas (for example: Development areas, explicit ramp-up, skills to build, training plan). Those phrases are not skill categories; map items into professional groups such as tools, domains, or leadership as appropriate."
    - "When items relate to engineering leadership, operating model, governance, ways of working, or operations, and the CV already has a group whose title clearly covers that theme (for example a title containing both leadership and operating model, or close synonyms), merge those items into that existing group instead of creating separate groups named Leadership, Management, Operations, or duplicates of the same theme."
    - "If the CV text ends with a short list introduced as candidate-requested or additional skills, treat every line as skill tokens only; fold them into existing groups as above, not as a new document section with its own heading."

  output_requirements:
    format: "JSON only matching the provided schema (optimized_structured_cv)."
    constraints:
      - "Strictly adhere to all types and constraints in the schema."
      - "For numeric fields (e.g. score, confidence): use the scale in the schema (e.g. 0-100); do not use 0-10, 0-1, or decimals for percentages."
`,
